socket2: IPv6 multicast join/leave on QNX.

socket2 0.5.7 leaves join_multicast_v6()/leave_multicast_v6() out on QNX
because it imports IPV6_ADD_MEMBERSHIP/IPV6_DROP_MEMBERSHIP, names QNX does
not use. QNX has the BSD names, IPV6_JOIN_GROUP/IPV6_LEAVE_GROUP (12/13 in
<netinet6/in6.h>, exported by libc), so alias them as socket2 already does
for the BSDs, and build the two functions. zenoh-link-udp calls them.

This is what socket2 upstream does since (target_os = "nto" in the
IPV6_JOIN_GROUP alias list); backported to 0.5.7, the version zenoh-c's
Cargo.lock pins, by ports/zenoh-c/recipe.sh.

Upstream-Status: Backport

